=== 1. DOES XGBOOST DEPEND ON COLUMN ORDER? (found while cross-checking two logs) ===
The panel scored standardised RFE-12 + XGBoost at 140/143; a second script that asked for
the same twelve columns in alphabetical order rather than file order scored 139/143.
Same rows, same hyper-parameters, same seed. This is that check, on both scales.
  native / file order      140/143  AUC 0.9931
  native / alphabetical    140/143  AUC 0.9963
  scaled / file order      140/143  AUC 0.9931
  scaled / alphabetical    140/143  AUC 0.9963
  native / file order      vs native / alphabetical    max|dp| 0.14517, labels differ on 0 of 143, counts 140 vs 140
  scaled / file order      vs scaled / alphabetical    max|dp| 0.14517, labels differ on 0 of 143, counts 140 vs 140
  trees whose text differs between the two column orders (same scale): 100 of 100 native, 100 of 100 scaled
  seeds 0/1/2/42 under the alphabetical scaled order: 140, 140, 140, 140

